# Known Pitfalls — {{PROJECT}}

> **Format:** one entry per pitfall. Severity → Symptom → Root cause → Mitigation → How we found it.
> **Maintenance:** add a new entry when something bites you — a level-2 heading written exactly as
> `## P-NN — Title` (never `### P-NN`) AND an Index row; the lint rejects a heading without its row.
> Don't trim — entries decay naturally and the dates stay honest. Never edit an existing entry;
> append a dated correction. Record both the symptom and the cause: symptoms usually point away
> from causes. Never invent a cause: evidence must contain the claimed event; label reported events
> when raw output is unavailable, and never cite a rule or an unrelated history entry as proof of a run.
> **Companion (code-level production issues):** `{{MEMORY_DIR}}/issues/ISSUE-NNN_*.md` (outside the repo; Claude Code auto-memory).
> **Next free ID: P-1** (recompute from the headings before assigning).

